From: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 07:06:20 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] arm64: dts: apple: t6050-k114-k116: report the built-in
 panel as eDP

The K114c and K116c panel is a simpledrm framebuffer until DCP drives it,
and its connector shows up as Unknown-1. Omarchy treats a connector that
is not eDP, LVDS or DSI as an external monitor and holds a block inhibitor
on handle-lid-switch, so closing the lid never suspends.

The previous commit makes simpledrm report eDP for a framebuffer node that
carries apple,internal-panel. Put the property on the shared K114/K116
framebuffer node, as the J714c node already has it.

Compile check only: the K114c dtb builds and dtc shows the property on
framebuffer@0; simpledrm.o builds. Not booted on a K114c yet.

Signed-off-by: Joshua Warren <816217+joshuaswarren@users.noreply.github.com>

(cherry picked from commit 76c5ea390d74c77fab63fb7a1ad98a7013ee386f)
[k114s: from aurora-silicon/linux pull request 1688 (open draft), unchanged]
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-k114-k116.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-k114-k116.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-k114-k116.dtsi
index 9758c90ed..bc21e6221 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-k114-k116.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-k114-k116.dtsi
@@ -47,6 +47,7 @@ framebuffer0: framebuffer@0 {
 			reg = <0 0 0 0>; /* To be filled by the loader */
 			/* Format properties will be added by the loader */
 			status = "disabled";
+			apple,internal-panel; /* simpledrm reports it as eDP */
 		};
 	};
 
